        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "OL09-00-000256 - OL 9 must display the Standard Mandatory DOD Notice and Consent Banner before granting local or remote access to the system via a SSH logon."
          info        : "The warning message reinforces policy awareness during the logon process and facilitates possible legal action against attackers. Alternatively, systems whose ownership should not be obvious should ensure usage of a banner that does not provide easy attribution.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000023-GPOS-00006, SRG-OS-000228-GPOS-00088"
          solution    : "Configure OL 9 to display the Standard Mandatory DOD Notice and Consent Banner before granting access to the system via ssh.

Edit the \"etc/ssh/sshd_config\" file or a file in \"/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d\" to uncomment the banner keyword and configure it to point to a file that will contain the logon banner (this file may be named differently or be in a different location if using a version of SSH that is provided by a third-party vendor).

An example configuration line is:

Banner /etc/issue"
