    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "OL09-00-000401 - OL 9 must be configured so that the pcscd socket is active."
      info        : "The information system ensures that even if the information system is compromised, that compromise will not affect credentials stored on the authentication device.

The daemon program for pcsc-lite and the MuscleCard framework is pcscd. It is a resource manager that coordinates communications with smart card readers and smart cards and cryptographic tokens that are connected to the system."
      solution    : "Enable the pcscd socket by running the following command:

$ sudo systemctl enable --now pcscd.socket"
      reference   : "800-171|3.5.1,800-171r3|03.05.01a.,800-53|IA-2(6),800-53r5|IA-2(6)(a),CAT|II,CCI|CCI-004046,CN-L3|7.1.3.1(a),CN-L3|7.1.3.1(e),CN-L3|8.1.4.1(a),CN-L3|8.1.4.2(a),CN-L3|8.5.4.1(a),CSF|PR.AC-1,CSF2.0|PR.AA-01,CSF2.0|PR.AA-03,DISA_Benchmark|Oracle_Linux_9_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(i),HIPAA|164.312(d),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.16,ITSG-33|IA-2(6),NESA|T2.3.8,NESA|T5.3.1,NESA|T5.4.2,NESA|T5.5.1,NESA|T5.5.2,NESA|T5.5.3,NIAv2|AM2,NIAv2|AM8,NIAv2|AM14b,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-271516r1208722_rule,STIG-ID|OL09-00-000401,SWIFT-CSCv1|4.2,TBA-FIISB|35.1,TBA-FIISB|36.1,Vuln-ID|V-271516"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_Oracle_Linux_9_V1R6_STIG.zip"
