    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "OL09-00-000940 - OL 9 must use the CAC smart card driver."
      info        : "Smart card login provides two-factor authentication stronger than that provided by a username and password combination. Smart cards leverage public key infrastructure to provide and verify credentials. Configuring the smart card driver in use by the organization helps to prevent users from using unauthorized smart cards.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000104-GPOS-00051, SRG-OS-000106-GPOS-00053, SRG-OS-000107-GPOS-00054, SRG-OS-000109-GPOS-00056, SRG-OS-000108-GPOS-00055, SRG-OS-000112-GPOS-00057, SRG-OS-000113-GPOS-00058"
      solution    : "Configure OL 9 to load the CAC driver.

Add or modify the following line in the \"/etc/opensc.conf\" file:

card_drivers = cac;"
