      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "OL09-00-001110 - OL 9 must not allow blank or null passwords."
          info        : "If an account has an empty password, anyone could log in and run commands with the privileges of that account. Accounts with empty passwords should never be used in operational environments."
          solution    : "Remove any instances of the \"nullok\" option in the \"/etc/pam.d/password-auth\" and \"/etc/pam.d/system-auth\" files to prevent logons with empty passwords.

Note: Manual changes to the listed file may be overwritten by the \"authselect\" program."
          reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|I,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,DISA_Benchmark|Oracle_Linux_9_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-271634r1091614_rule,STIG-ID|OL09-00-001110,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-271634"
          see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_Oracle_Linux_9_V1R6_STIG.zip"
