    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "OL09-00-002343 - OL 9 SSHD must not allow blank passwords."
      info        : "If an account has an empty password, anyone could log on and run commands with the privileges of that account. Accounts with empty passwords should never be used in operational environments."
      solution    : "Configure OL 9 to prevent SSH users from logging on with blank passwords by editing the following line in \"/etc/ssh/sshd_config\" or in a file in \"/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d\":

PermitEmptyPasswords no

Restart the SSH daemon for the settings to take effect:

$ sudo systemctl restart sshd.service"
