    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "OL09-00-002345 - OL 9 must not permit direct logons to the root account using remote access via SSH."
      info        : "Even though the communications channel may be encrypted, an additional layer of security is gained by extending the policy of not logging directly on as root. In addition, logging in with a user-specific account provides individual accountability of actions performed on the system and also helps to minimize direct attack attempts on root's password."
      solution    : "Configure OL 9 to prevent SSH users from logging on directly as root by adding or modifying the following line in \"/etc/ssh/sshd_config\" or in a file in \"/etc/ssh/sshd_config.d\".

PermitRootLogin no

Restart the SSH daemon for the settings to take effect:

$ sudo systemctl restart sshd.service"
