    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "OL09-00-002370 - OL 9 must disable the use of user namespaces."
      info        : "User namespaces are used primarily for Linux containers. The value \"0\" disallows the use of user namespaces."
      solution    : "Configure OL 9 to disable the use of user namespaces by adding the following line to a file, in the \"/etc/sysctl.d\" directory:

Note: User namespaces are used primarily for Linux containers. If containers are in use, this requirement is Not Applicable.

user.max_user_namespaces = 0

The system configuration files need to be reloaded for the changes to take effect. To reload the contents of the files, run the following command:

$ sudo sysctl --system"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,DISA_Benchmark|Oracle_Linux_9_STIG,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-271727r1091893_rule,STIG-ID|OL09-00-002370,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-271727"
      see_also    : "https://dl.dod.cyber.mil/wp-content/uploads/stigs/zip/U_Oracle_Linux_9_V1R6_STIG.zip"
      cmd         : "/sbin/sysctl user.max_user_namespaces"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*user\\.max_user_namespaces[\\s]*=[\\s]*0[\\s]*$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "OL09-00-002376 - OL 9 must terminate idle user sessions."
      info        : "Terminating an idle session within a short time period reduces the window of opportunity for unauthorized personnel to take control of a management session enabled on the console or console port that has been left unattended."
      solution    : "Configure OL 9 to log out idle sessions by editing the /etc/systemd/logind.conf file with the following line:

StopIdleSessionSec=600

