    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "OL09-00-003020 - OL 9 must automatically lock an account when three unsuccessful logon attempts occur."
      info        : "By limiting the number of failed logon attempts, the risk of unauthorized system access via user password guessing, otherwise known as brute-force attacks, is reduced. Limits are imposed by locking the account.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000329-GPOS-00128, SRG-OS-000021-GPOS-00005"
      solution    : "Configure OL 9 to lock an account when three unsuccessful logon attempts occur.

Add/modify the \"/etc/security/faillock.conf\" file to match the following line:

deny = 3"
